ow many  more times  painful it is compared to a normal  period cramp  but like period cramps kind of like your  insides are being  twisted um and also it's exhausting like  i remember  going through like with my doula going  through like exercises breathing  exercises to try to get through each  contraction  and like my legs would be shaking by the  end and i was in really good shape then  i was spinning like every day so  i was physically exhausted and drained  by the the kind of marathon that is  labor  and i really don't know what pushing  like the sensation of the  what they call the ring of fire feels  like because i had an epidural at that  point  and i also don't know what tearing feels  like because i didn't tear  what i do want moms to do and to know is  to not  be afraid um i actually cannot wait for  labor again it was so exciting  you know even the pain of it that those  kind of memories almost fade away  because  the pushing part like that hour of  pushing was the most exciting  exhilarating hour of my life  it was literally like having a room full  of supportive people  cheering you on telling you you're  amazing telling you how strong you are  and how awesome that push was like it  was so  so exciting and and even though i had a  bit of a like traumatic post birth  experience where  i had the postpartum hemorrhage and i  had the retained placenta and the  pushing and the  beating of on my belly thinking about  those things  is a little bit scary but the pushing  experience and just  the adrenaline rush and holding the baby  in your arms afterwards  it was so so amazing and as soon as i as  soon as it happened as soon as the baby  came out i said i turned to my husband i  said  can we do that again because it was just  it was just so cool  the whole experience was just so cool so  yeah don't be afraid  it was the experience is just so  incredibly  fun okay next question what will my  postpartum diet  look like honestly probably like  whatever  i feel like and also probably a lot of  it i was super hungry last time when i  was breastfeeding and i  expect things will be the same this time  um but yeah probably a lot of soups i  froze  i've i've already frozen like 15 bags of  homemade soup in the freezer so i'll  probably be having a lot of that because  i know last time i was craving a lot of  you know hydration and water so that was  really key  um also i ate a lot of watermelon so  this time at least watermelon will be  more in season so i'll probably have a  lot of that  and then lots of snacks right like tons  of  nuts and bars i love kind bars i always  had those  i love dips so hummus and guacamole  higher calorie snacks like that  that are really easy to to reach for and  grab  and also yogurt i mean i love yogurt and  greek yogurt  even when i'm not breastfeeding and  nursing so probably a lot of yogurt  because i also know that my protein and  my  calcium needs are going to be extra high  while nursing so  those are the kind of things that i'm  probably going to be eating a lot of  things that are really super easy to  grab  and just shove in my face really quickly  because i'm probably not going to have a  whole lot of time for super fancy meals  have you been exercising during your  pregnancy  yes actually and i think there's a huge  misconception that you you can't  exercise and i actually address this in  my  pregnancy myth video but honestly not a  whole lot has changed my exercise regime  um i'm not doing hit workouts obviously  and i never  really was i haven't for a long time at  least because a i don't enjoy them and b  you know even before i was pregnant it  just wasn't really great for my  fertility  um but i walk daily either inside on the  treadmill on an  incline or outside with my husband and  my kid  so i try to enjoy the outdoors while i  can and it's not too hot and my hands  aren't blowing up  um but i'm also doing like a combination  of strength training like weight lifting  and like bar workouts sometimes with my  virtual trainer  and sometimes i do a lot of like um  youtube videos so i love  sydney cummings videos if you are not  familiar with her  youtube workouts they're amazing so  definitely check that out but of course  i'm always interested in hearing  some other great youtubers that you love  to to to follow along with their  workouts so leave me some comments and  ideas below  but yeah i don't do a lot of ab stuff  definitely not like any like twisting  moves  um i have diastasis recti from my first  pregnancy and a little bit of prolapse  so i definitely don't want to make that  any worse in this pregnancy if i can  avoid it  um and i don't do any workout moves that  really get me  out of breath so definitely less  compound moves  more kind of static arms a lot of booty  band  moves things like that a lot of back  exercises  because honestly pregnancy and  breastfeeding both kind of get you to  like  slump over which is not a great look not  great for my posture  um but yeah i just feel best when i'm  exercising it  definitely helps with energy levels and  it definitely helps with sleep  and digestion so i do try to keep  active in pregnancy okay last question  how is big boy e feeling about the baby  and being a big brother  so he's so cute he's so affectionate he  will come up to me  and like hug my belly and say mama's  baby  and give it a kiss and stroke it very  gently he knows to be very gentle  he's actually gonna be a really great  big brother because  you know as far as boys go he's very  affectionate i know everyone complains  oh boys are so wild  not my boy my boys is a very loving he  loves to cuddle he loves his teddies and  his  his baby doll that we we've been  practicing on  um i expect that he may be a little bit  jealous in an attention-grabbing kind of  way because  in all honesty he has been a little  spoiled in kova times because mommy and  daddy have been around a lot more  so he's had a lot more of us to to  to spend time with us more often um and  also he's into this like game where he  calls mommy mommy mommy mommy mommy  mommy mommy mommy mommy  until you kind of acknowledge him same  with daddy doesn't matter whoever is  around he will just call  on repeat um and so i expect that might  get worse but we'll see  but one little quick tip that my mom  gave me because i think i mentioned  that my mother was a montessori teacher  so she's been dealing with young  children her whole life  and she told me a trick that she used  that they would use in the school  where they would teach the children to  put their hand on the adult's shoulder  when they want their attention  and when the adult was ready for them  they would you know turn to them and nod  to them and say  yes so and so um and that's how  they were being taught patients and so  we're trying that with my son he's still  a little bit young to totally embrace it  but i think he's gonna get it before the  baby comes  so i'm hoping that we're gonna build up  some of those patience skills  before baby number two comes but  honestly i'm not worried i'm not worried  about him hurting the baby  i'm not worried about him getting you  know throwing too many tantrums he's  just  very affectionate and and gentle in his  nature  so i know he's going to be an amazing  big brother  well folks i'm going to go enjoy the  outside you can see the sun is just like  beaming on me and it's getting really  hot in here  um not the most flattering light that's  for sure but  i'm going to go enjoy the day and on  that note uh if you like this video  don't forget to give it the thumbs up  don't forget to subscribe and ring the  little bell so you never miss a video  um also leave me comments below if you  have any questions about pregnancy  postpartum  breastfeeding i'm definitely gonna be  talking a lot more about breastfeeding  after this baby comes so  be prepared for that and i will see you  next time on abby's kitchen  bye
 

